/scripts/               @D3V0N5H1R3

# ── Vendored third-party code: intentionally UNOWNED ──
# A bare pattern (no owner) removes code-owner review, so routine
# vendored-dependency bumps don't require maintainer sign-off. This
# covers the genuinely third-party trees under external/: lit-html,
# lucide, mbedtls, miniz, pico-css, uplot, and webview.
/external/

# First-party code that happens to live under external/ IS owned. These
# more-specific rules override the blanket /external/ rule above (last
# match wins):
#   - gui-framework/ : the project's own GraphicalUi renderer and charts
#     (JS/CSS/tests), which has its own CI gate (ci-gui-framework.yml).
#   - DIRECTORY.md      : the project's own doc describing the vendored deps.
/external/gui-framework/  @D3V0N5H1R3
/external/DIRECTORY.md       @D3V0N5H1R3
